What is MLOPS

	MLOps (Machine Learning Operations) is the discipline that combines machine learning with DevOps practices to ensure ML models are not just built, but also reliably deployed, monitored, and maintained in production environments. Think of it as the bridge between data science experiments and real-world applications.



	What MLOps Is

		A set of practices for managing the ML lifecycle end-to-end.

		Ensures scalability, reproducibility, and automation of ML workflows.

		Focuses on collaboration between data scientists, ML engineers, and operations teams.


	Core Components of MLOps

		Version Control

			Track code, data, and models (Git, DVC).

		Experiment Tracking

			Log parameters, metrics, and artifacts (MLflow, W&B).

		Pipeline Orchestration

			Automate workflows (Kubeflow, Airflow, ZenML).

		Model Deployment

			Serve models via APIs, batch jobs, or cloud endpoints.

		Monitoring & Maintenance

			Detect drift, track latency, trigger retraining (Evidently AI, Prometheus).

		CI/CD for ML

			Continuous integration and deployment of models, just like software.

		Governance & Compliance

			Audit trails, reproducibility, and responsible AI practices.

	Why MLOps Matters

		Before MLOps: Models live in notebooks, hard to reproduce, fragile deployments.

		After MLOps: Models are versioned, deployed automatically, monitored continuously, and retrained when needed.


Simple Analogy

	Data Scientist: Builds the recipe (model).

	ML Engineer: Makes sure the recipe can be cooked at scale.

	MLOps: Runs the kitchen — automating cooking, serving, and checking quality every day.


How is MLOps different from DevOps?


	DevOps

		Focus: Software development and operations.

		Goal: Deliver applications quickly, reliably, and continuously.

		Practices:

		Continuous Integration (CI) → automated builds and tests.

		Continuous Deployment (CD) → automated releases to production.

		Infrastructure as Code → reproducible environments.

		Monitoring & Logging → system health and uptime.

	MLOps

		Focus: Machine learning lifecycle in production.

		Goal: Deliver ML models that are reproducible, scalable, and continuously improving.

		Practices:

		Data Versioning → track datasets and features.

		Experiment Tracking → log parameters, metrics, artifacts.

		Model Registry → manage versions and approvals.

		CI/CD for ML → automate training, testing, and deployment of models.

		Monitoring & Retraining → detect drift, trigger retraining pipelines.

		Governance → audit trails, compliance, reproducibility.


	Simple Analogy

		DevOps: Keeps the software factory running smoothly.

		MLOps: Runs the AI kitchen, ensuring recipes (models) are versioned, cooked (trained), served (deployed), and tasted (monitored) continuously.


