Machine learning lifecycle overview 

	Data → Preparation → Training → Evaluation → Deployment → Monitoring → Retraining


	Data Collection
		
		Gather raw data from sources (databases, APIs, sensors, logs).

		Ensure data relevance and sufficient volume.

	Data Preparation

		Clean missing values, handle outliers, normalize/standardize.

		Split into training, validation, and test sets.

		Feature engineering to extract meaningful signals.

	Model Selection

		Choose algorithms based on problem type (classification, regression, clustering).

		Consider trade-offs: accuracy vs interpretability vs scalability.


	Model Training


		Fit the model on training data.

		Tune hyperparameters for optimal performance.

		Use cross-validation to reduce overfitting.

	Model Evaluation

		Assess performance using metrics:

		Classification → Accuracy, Precision, Recall, F1, ROC-AUC.

		Regression → MSE, MAE, R².

		Compare against baselines.

	Model Deployment

		Package model (Pickle, ONNX, TorchScript).

		Serve via APIs (FastAPI, Flask) or batch pipelines.

		Containerize with Docker/Kubernetes for scalability.


	Monitoring & Maintenance

		Track model drift, latency, and accuracy in production.

		Set up alerts and dashboards (Prometheus, Grafana, Evidently AI).

		Retrain periodically or when drift is detected.


